# COPENHAGEN PLANK

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Copenhagen Plank is an isometric lateral core exercise designed to develop adductor strength, pelvic stability and frontal-plane control.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the highest-value exercises for improving groin robustness and reducing adductor injury risk.

---

# Philosophy

Combat athletes constantly generate force laterally.

Changing direction.

Kicking.

Sprawling.

Passing guard.

Escaping positions.

These actions place substantial stress on the adductors.

CAS selects the Copenhagen Plank to increase frontal-plane stability and improve long-term athlete durability.

